{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 104,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Bless the LORD, O my soul! O LORD my God, You are very great; You are clothed with splendor and majesty.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He wraps Himself in light as with a garment; He stretches out the heavens like a tent,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "laying the beams of His chambers in the waters above, making the clouds His chariot, walking on the wings of the wind.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He makes the winds His messengers, flames of fire His servants.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He set the earth on its foundations, never to be moved.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You covered it with the deep like a garment; the waters stood above the mountains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "At Your rebuke the waters fled; at the sound of Your thunder they hurried away —",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "the mountains rose and the valleys sank to the place You assigned for them —",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You set a boundary they cannot cross, that they may never again cover the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He sends forth springs in the valleys; they flow between the mountains.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "They give drink to every beast of the field; the wild donkeys quench their thirst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The birds of the air nest beside the springs; they sing among the branches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He waters the mountains from His chambers; the earth is satisfied by the fruit of His works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He makes the grass grow for the livestock and provides crops for man to cultivate, bringing forth food from the earth:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "wine that gladdens the heart of man, oil that makes his face to shine, and bread that sustains his heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The trees of the LORD have their fill, the cedars of Lebanon that He planted,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "where the birds build their nests; the stork makes her home in the cypresses.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The high mountains are for the wild goats, the cliffs a refuge for the rock badgers.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He made the moon to mark the seasons; the sun knows when to set.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "You bring darkness, and it becomes night, when all the beasts of the forest prowl.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The young lions roar for their prey and seek their food from God.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sun rises, and they withdraw; they lie down in their dens.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man goes forth to his work and to his labor until evening.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How many are Your works, O LORD! In wisdom You have made them all; the earth is full of Your creatures.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Here is the sea, vast and wide, teeming with creatures beyond number, living things both great and small.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There the ships pass, and Leviathan, which You formed to frolic there.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All creatures look to You to give them their food in due season.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When You give it to them, they gather it up; when You open Your hand, they are satisfied with good things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When You hide Your face, they are terrified; when You take away their breath, they die and return to dust.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When You send Your Spirit, they are created, and You renew the face of the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May the glory of the LORD endure forever; may the LORD rejoice in His works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He looks on the earth, and it trembles; He touches the mountains, and they smolder.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will sing to the LORD all my life; I will sing praise to my God while I have my being.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May my meditation be pleasing to Him, for I rejoice in the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.104.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PSA.104.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "May sinners vanish from the earth and the wicked be no more. Bless the LORD, O my soul. Hallelujah!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
